Reason for Referral/Chief Complaint\plain\f4\fs22 : Presents to therapy with persisting visual challenges, persistent left head-ache, and on-set of severe frontal HA/nausea with sustained visual focus/concentration. Pt reports did make progress for a 
while following concussion but progress plateaued about a year ago. Previously started course of vision therapy at New Horizons, however discontinued about halfway through 12 course session due to frustration with exercises/progress. Pt more recently 
completed intake at Vision Therapy Center and will be scheduling course of therapy soon. Pt has glasses with binasal taping though Pt reports tape very thin/does not appear to block any visual input. \par 
\par 
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\b Onset\plain\f4\fs22 : ~2 years ago\par 
\li1\ltrpar\ql\plain\f0\fs22\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\b Mechanism of Injury/ Issues\plain\f4\fs22 : \par 
Per EMR: \par 
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\i Joshua Craig Mandel is a 39 year old male with a history of mild TBI who presents today to the UW Rehabilitation Clinic for a consultation. \line\line He states that back in 7/2020 he had hit 
head on the bike rack attached to car while closing the trunk. Denies any PTA or LOC at the time and he was able to drive home without issues. Soon aferward he went to go on bike ride without tipping over but endorsed feeling nauseated with a headache. 
He was able to get home without issues afterward. He would Tylenol or Ibuprofen as needed but uses these medications very sparingly. Since his initial injury he states that he feels he has recovered approximately 90-95% but continues to have issues with 
his vision, headaches, and nausea.\line\line He is well educated having graduated from Tufts Medical School and MIT for engineering and currently works with heath data interoperability with Microsoft.\line His work is computer based and staring at screens 
will bring on his headaches, difficulty concentrating, and nausea at times.\line He has since adapted to his by taking frequent breaks from the computer screen to rest his eyes. \line He denies having any extended leave from work and is currently working 
full time from home.\~\plain\f4\fs22\par 
